 "capsule": "The First Portuguese Republic, proclaimed on 5 October 1910 after the overthrow of the Braganza monarchy, was organized under the 1911 constitution as a secular parliamentary state with a weak presidency and dominant National Assembly. Chronic cabinet instability - roughly 45 governments in sixteen years - combined with financial crisis, labor unrest, and the strains of Portugal's costly entry into World War I to discredit parliamentary rule. On 28 May 1926 a military coup led by General Gomes da Costa overthrew the republic, opening the way to the Ditadura Nacional and eventually Salazar's Estado Novo.",
